			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1559220">
									

<blockquote>
<p>tale pages are stories, narratives, and transcripts that are written in a non-scientific manner, as well as incident logs, interviews, and reports that are not directly linked to by a scp page. These may not necessarily be about any particular scp, and may not even be about a scp that exists, but should otherwise exist within the SCP Foundation universe. A tale page cannot be a creepypasta page at the same time. (Compare to creepypasta, below.)</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>creepypasta are short stories or narratives in the form of urban legends or urban myths. These are usually but not necessarily completely unrelated to the SCP Foundation, and usually take the form of killer-in-your-house stories and other creepy stories. A creepypasta page cannot be a tale page at the same time. (Compare to tale, above.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not as far as the tag guide is concerned, a page cannot be both a tale and a creepypasta or vice-versa</p>

